#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# permanent

#% text
# `permanent(m)` gives the permanent of the matrix `m`, the sum over all permutations of the products of the chosen entries without signs.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is computed by Ryser's formula in `2^n` steps for an `n` by `n` matrix.

#% item
# For a rectangular matrix with fewer rows than columns it is the sum of the permanents of the square submatrices on all choices of columns.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
permanent([[1, 2], [3, 4]])
#% output
#= 10

#% cell
permanent([[a, b], [c, d]])
#% output
#= a*d + b*c

#% cell
permanent([[1, 1, 1], [1, 1, 1], [1, 1, 1]])
#% output
#= 6

#% cell
permanent([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]])
#% output
#= 58

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `det`, `minors`
